# MissionDMX — raw USB access for DMX adapters.
#
# Enttec DMX USB Pro ships with the stock FTDI FT232 VID:PID 0403:6001
# (confirmed against the Project-Editor sources in
# src/controller/file/serializing/universe_serialization.py:71 and
# src/view/dialogs/universe_dialog.py:23-24). fish talks to it via
# libftdi1 + libusb1 (see meta-custom/recipes-mdmx/realtime-fish/
# realtime-fish_git.bb:35-55), i.e. by opening /dev/bus/usb/<bus>/<dev>
# directly rather than a /dev/ttyUSB* serial node — so chown'ing the
# raw USB node to dialout is what actually unblocks unprivileged fish.
# MODE=0660 + GROUP="dialout" matches mdmx-user.bb:18-19 which already
# puts the UI 'user' in dialout. TAG+="uaccess" lets logind-style
# sessions also claim it if one ever runs here.
#
# Side-effect note: this VID:PID is the generic FT232 pair, shared with
# other FTDI serial dongles. On this appliance fish is the only client
# of the FTDI stack, so broadening access to all FT232 devices is fine.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0403", ATTRS{idProduct}=="6001", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
